# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS / KEYS — NEVER commit these.
# A leaked cloud SSH private key or credential file is the single most common
# cause of a compromised VM being hijacked for crypto-mining => a runaway bill.
# These patterns make git refuse to stage them even by accident.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.pem            # AWS/Azure downloaded key pairs
*.key            # generic private keys
*.ppk            # PuTTY keys
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
id_ed25519
id_ed25519.*
*.pfx            # Azure certificate bundles
.env             # any local environment file with secrets
.env.*
azure.json       # Azure CLI / SDK credential dumps
*.credentials

# Compiled sentri binary (built locally on the Linux box, not committed)
/sentri

# The extracted Alpine root filesystem (Milestone 2) — large, machine-specific,
# and easy to re-fetch. We document HOW to obtain it in the README instead of
# committing it.
/rootfs/*
!/rootfs/.gitkeep

# The downloaded rootfs tarball itself (also re-fetchable, not source).
alpine-minirootfs-*.tar.gz
*.tar.gz

# Learned syscall baselines (Milestone 5) are generated artifacts.
/baselines/

# Editor / OS noise
*.swp
.DS_Store
